    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> became independent by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montevideo">Montevideo</a> of 1828, brokered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> through Viscount John Ponsonby after the 500-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war">Cisplatine War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and the United Provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>; its first constitution followed on 18 July 1830.</li><li>The Colorados and the Blancos fought the thirteen-year <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguayan-civil-war">Guerra Grande</a> (1839–1851), during which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montevideo">Montevideo</a> was besieged for nine years and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Garibaldi</a> led its Italian legion; their rivalry ended in a formula of co-participation after 1872.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-batlle-y-ordonez">José Batlle y Ordóñez</a>'s reforms (1903–1915) made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>'; a civic-military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> (1973–1985) gave it the world's highest proportion of political prisoners before democracy returned in 1985.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>On 11 December 2013 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> became the first country in the world to fully legalise the growth, use and sale of cannabis, by a Senate vote of 16 to 13, under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-mujica">José Mujica</a>, a former Tupamaro <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> who had spent almost fifteen years in prison.</p></aside>
    </section>

